VALUES (4600913104020129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Mathematics-IV requires the behaviour described by the syllabus area concerned with Concept. Explain how Concept applies, outline the main steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Mathematics-IV requires the behaviour described by the syllabus area concerned with Point : Distance formula. Explain how Point : Distance formula applies, outline the main steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Mathematics-IV requires the behaviour described by the syllabus area concerned with Definition and concept. Explain how Definition and concept applies, outline the main steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Mathematics-IV requires the behaviour described by the syllabus area concerned with Definition. Explain how Definition applies, outline the main steps and justify the result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Concept is covered under “Complex Number”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Geometric meaning of complex number, Modulus, Amplitude, Square root of complex numbers, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Geometric meaning of complex number; Modulus; Amplitude; Square root of complex numbers. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-IV problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Point : Distance formula is covered under “Co-ordinate Geometry”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Mid-point formula, Straight Line : Forms of equations of straight lines : Slope-Point form, Two points form, Intercept form, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Mid-point formula; Straight Line : Forms of equations of straight lines : Slope-Point form; Two points form; Intercept form. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-IV problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Integration accumulates a quantity or represents area under a curve. Definite integrals have bounds and the result''s units follow from the integrand and variable.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Some particular integrals; Integration by substitution method; Integration by parts; Integration by partial fraction (for linear factors). State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-IV problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** A differential equation relates a function to its derivatives. Solving it requires an appropriate method and, where supplied, initial or boundary conditions.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Order and degree of a differential equation; Solution of first order differential equation by Separable; Homogeneous and Integrating factor methods; Differential Equations (First Order First degree). State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-IV problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

