VALUES (460009382403015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Refrigeration”, how should Concept of refrigeration be applied? Explain the method, identify the governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Basic Utility”, how should List and use of various utilities in chemical plant be applied? Explain the method, identify the governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Refrigeration”, how should Brine. Selection of Refrigerants. be applied? Explain the method, identify the governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Basic Utility”, how should (ii) Zeolite process be applied? Explain the method, identify the governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Concept of refrigeration is listed under “Refrigeration” in the syllabus. Define the concept, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Refrigeration, Methods of Refrigeration: (i) Ice Refrigeration, (ii) Evaporative Refrigeration, (iii) Vapor Refrigeration System. COP and TOR of refrigeration. Types of Primary Refrigerant, and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant variables or assumptions and describe a check for the result and a limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Refrigeration; Methods of Refrigeration: (i) Ice Refrigeration; (ii) Evaporative Refrigeration; (iii) Vapor Refrigeration System. COP and TOR of refrigeration. Types of Primary Refrigerant. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete PLANT UTILIZATION AND INSTRUMENTATION problem from “Refrigeration”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** List and use of various utilities in chemical plant is listed under “Basic Utility” in the syllabus. Define the concept, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Basic Utility, Sources of water, Types of Water, Hard & Soft water, and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant variables or assumptions and describe a check for the result and a limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Basic Utility; Sources of water; Types of Water; Hard & Soft water. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete PLANT UTILIZATION AND INSTRUMENTATION problem from “Basic Utility”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Brine. Selection of Refrigerants. is listed under “Refrigeration” in the syllabus. Define the concept, explain its role and main process/design s