INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4600093824030129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain and apply List and use of various utilities in chemical plant in “Basic Utility”, including the principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Utilities: Use of Steam in “Steam, Air & Inert Gases”, including the principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Concept of refrigeration in “Refrigeration”, including the principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Importance of instrumentation in chemical plant. Classification of instruments in “Basics of Instrumentation”, including the principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** List and use of various utilities in chemical plant is included in “Basic Utility”. Define its role, describe its main steps/components, relate it to Sources of water, Types of Water, Hard & Soft water, Boiler Feed water and demineralized water. Methods of water softening processes (i) Lime soda process (Hot & Cold), give an application and a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Sources of water, Types of Water, Hard & Soft water, Boiler Feed water and demineralized water. Methods of water softening processes (i) Lime soda process (Hot & Cold).\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical PLANT UTILIZATION AND INSTRUMENTATION task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state one limitation or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Utilities: Use of Steam is included in “Steam, Air & Inert Gases”. Define its role, describe its main steps/components, relate it to Air & Inert Gases as utilities, Types of Air compressors Reciprocating Air compressors (i) Multistage compressors (ii) Rotary compressors, Steam, Air & Inert Gases, give an application and a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Air & Inert Gases as utilities, Types of Air compressors Reciprocating Air compressors (i) Multistage compressors (ii) Rotary compressors, Steam, Air & Inert Gases.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical PLANT UTILIZATION AND INSTRUMENTATION task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state one limitation or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Concept of refrigeration is included in “Refrigeration”. Define its role, describe its main steps/components, relate it to Methods of Refrigeration: (i) Ice Refrigeration, (ii) Evaporative Refrigeration, (iii) Vapor Refrigeration System. COP and TOR of refrigeration. Types of Primary Refrigerants: Ammonia, Halo Carbons (Freon of Different type), give an application and a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Methods of Refrigeration: (i) Ice Refrigeration, (ii) Evaporative Refrigeration, (iii) Vapor Refrigeration System. COP and TOR of refrigeration. Types of Primary Refrigerants: Ammonia, Halo Carbons (Freon of Different type).\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical PLANT UTILIZATION AND INSTRUMENTATION task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state one limitation or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Importance of instrumentation in chemical plant. Classification of instruments is included in “Basics of Instrumentation”. Define its role, describe its main steps/components, relate it to Basic elements of instruments, Static and Dynamic Characteristics of instruments, First order system and second order system ., Basics of Instrumentation, give an application and a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Basic elements of instruments, Static and Dynamic Characteristics of instruments, First order system and second order system ., Basics of Instrumentation.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical PLANT UTILIZATION AND INSTRUMENTATION task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state one limitation or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

