INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4600093824020129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain and apply Definition of Heat Transfer and its importance in process industries in “Introduction to Heat Transfer”, including the principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Fourier s law of heat conduction with Concepts of (a) Heat transfer rate (b) Heat flux ( in “Heat Transfer by Conduction.”, including the principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Types of Convection in “Heat Transfer by Convection.”, including the principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Types of heat exchanger in “Heat exchangers”, including the principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Definition of Heat Transfer and its importance in process industries is included in “Introduction to Heat Transfer”. Define its role, describe its main steps/components, relate it to Classification of modes of heat transfer, Differentiation of steady and unsteady state of heat transfer., Introduction to Heat Transfer, give an application and a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Classification of modes of heat transfer, Differentiation of steady and unsteady state of heat transfer., Introduction to Heat Transfer.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical PROCESS HEAT TRANSFER task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state one limitation or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Conduction transfers heat through material without bulk movement of the material.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Thermal conductivity. Steady state (S.S.) heat conduction through composite wall, S.S. heat conduction through composite cylinder up to three layers, S.S. heat conduction through composite sphere up to three layers, Simple problems by direct use formula. Thermal Conductivity of solids.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical PROCESS HEAT TRANSFER task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state one limitation or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Convection transfers heat between a surface and a moving fluid; it may be natural or forced.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Free convection, Force convection. Newton s Law of convective heat transfer. Individual and Overall heat transfer coefficient. Simple Problems of Convection Simple Problems of Convection, Heat Transfer by Convection..\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical PROCESS HEAT TRANSFER task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state one limitation or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** A heat exchanger transfers energy between fluids, generally through a separating wall; area, temperature difference and heat-transfer coefficient affect duty.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Double pipe heat exchanger (a) Counter current (b) Co-current, Shell and tube heat exchanger: (a) 1-1 Pass (b) 1-2 Pass (c) 2-4 Pass, Plate type heat exchanger, Finned type (extended surface) heat exchanger.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical PROCESS HEAT TRANSFER task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state one limitation or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

