VALUES (460009382401015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids”, how should Effect of temperature / pressure& concentration on diffusivity be applied? Explain the method, identify the governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids”, how should Rate of diffusion in Mass Transfer be applied? Explain the method, identify the governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids”, how should Definition of diffusivity and concentration gradient be applied? Explain the method, identify the governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids”, how should Difference between molecular & turbulent /Eddy diffusion be applied? Explain the method, identify the governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Effect of temperature / pressure& concentration on diffusivity is listed under “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids” in the syllabus. Define the concept, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Molecular Diffusion in Fluids, Definition of Diffusion (a) Molecular diffusion (b) Eddy diffusion, Difference between molecular & turbulent /Eddy diffusion, Rate of diffusion in Mass Transfer, and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant variables or assumptions and describe a check for the result and a limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Molecular Diffusion in Fluids; Definition of Diffusion (a) Molecular diffusion (b) Eddy diffusion; Difference between molecular & turbulent /Eddy diffusion; Rate of diffusion in Mass Transfer. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete UNIT OPERATION - III problem from “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Rate of diffusion in Mass Transfer is listed under “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids” in the syllabus. Define the concept, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Molecular Diffusion in Fluids, Definition of Diffusion (a) Molecular diffusion (b) Eddy diffusion, Difference between molecular & turbulent /Eddy diffusion, Statement of Fick s first law for diffusivity, and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant variables or assumptions and describe a check for the result and a limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Molecular Diffusion in Fluids; Definition of Diffusion (a) Molecular diffusion (b) Eddy diffusion; Difference between molecular & turbulent /Eddy diffusion; Statement of Fick s first law for diffusivity. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete UNIT OPERATION - III problem from “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Definition of diffusivity and concentration gradient is listed under “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids” in the syllabus. Define the concept, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Molecular Diffusion in Fluids, Definition of Diffusion (a) Molecular diffusion (b) Eddy diffusion, Difference between molecular & turbulent /Eddy diffusion, Rate of diffusion in Mass Transfer, and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant variables or assumptions and describe a check for the result and a limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Molecular Diffusion in Fluids; Definition of Diffusion (a) Molecular diffusion (b) Eddy diffusion; Difference between molecular & turbulent /Eddy diffusion; Rate of diffusion in Mass Transfer. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete UNIT OPERATION - III problem from “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Difference between molecular & turbulent /Eddy diffusion is listed under “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids” in the syllabus. Define the concept, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Molecular Diffusion in Fluids, Definition of Diffusion (a) Molecular diffusion (b) Eddy diffusion, Rate of diffusion in Mass Transfer, Statement of Fick s first law for diffusivity, and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant variables or assumptions and describe a check for the result and a limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Molecular Diffusion in Fluids; Definition of Diffusion (a) Molecular diffusion (b) Eddy diffusion; Rate of diffusion in Mass Transfer; Statement of Fick s first law for diffusivity. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete UNIT OPERATION - III problem from “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

